<DocsLayout title="Xteink readers" description="Send reading sessions from an Xteink reader on CrossPoint or CrossInk firmware to Tome: which way to use, setup, and what arrives.">
  <SectionHero section="integrations" />
  <h1>Xteink readers (CrossPoint, CrossInk)</h1>
  <p>
    An Xteink reader can send its reading to Tome in two ways. Which one you can use depends
    on the firmware: <a href="https://github.com/crosspoint-reader/crosspoint-reader" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CrossPoint</a>{' '}
    2.0 has plugins, and <a href="https://github.com/uxjulia/CrossInk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CrossInk</a>{' '}
    2.0 has plugins and a sync of its own. Both are experimental in Tome.
  </p>
  <DocsMeta />

  <h2>Which one to use</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th></th><th>Built-in sync</th><th>Plugin</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Firmware</td><td>CrossInk 2.0 or newer</td><td>CrossPoint 2.0, CrossInk 2.0 or newer</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Sends</td><td>When you sync on the reader</td><td>By itself when the reader goes to sleep</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Reading time per session</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Progress</td><td>Yes, with the exact position</td><td>Yes, as a percentage</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pages</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Clippings</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Reading from before the first sync</td><td>Yes, as totals and reading days</td><td>No</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Tested on a device</td><td>Yes (Xteink X3)</td><td>Not yet</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>On CrossPoint:</strong> the plugin. It is the only way.</li>
    <li><strong>On CrossInk, for full stats:</strong> the built-in sync. It is the one with pages,
      clippings and exact positions, and the one that has run on a device.</li>
    <li><strong>On CrossInk, if you forget to sync:</strong> add the plugin next to the built-in
      sync. Sessions then arrive by themselves, and a session that comes both ways counts
      once. Pages still need a sync from the reader now and then.</li>
  </ul>
  <Callout variant="info" title="Moving from CrossPoint Sync?">
    Reading you already sent to CrossPoint Sync is not sent again. Export your account there and
    bring it in under <strong>Settings → Import reading history</strong>.
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="plugin">The plugin (CrossPoint 2.0 and CrossInk, experimental)</h2>
  <Callout variant="warning" title="Not tested on a device yet">
    The plugin has run in CrossInk's desktop simulator, which is the firmware's own code on a
    computer: the reader connected with its code, a book downloaded from Tome, read for a few
    pages, the reader put to sleep, the session delivered and shown on the book in Tome. CrossPoint 2.0.0's own delivery code has
    run the plugin on a computer too. Nobody has run it on an Xteink reader so far. If you
    try it, tell us how it went.
  </Callout>
  <p>
    With the plugin the reader sends each reading session to Tome by itself when it goes to
    sleep. You do not have to start a sync, and nothing is typed on the reader: you connect it
    by scanning a code from its screen.
  </p>
  <Steps>
    <li>In <strong>Settings → Xteink readers</strong>, choose <strong>Download plugin ZIP</strong>.</li>
    <li>Unpack it into the <code>plugins</code> folder on the reader's SD card, so that the
      card has a folder <code>/plugins/tome</code>.</li>
    <li>On the reader, turn on <strong>Plugins</strong> in the settings, open
      <strong>Plugins</strong> on Home and choose <strong>Tome</strong>. It says that a sign-in
      is required; choose <strong>Sign in</strong>.</li>
    <li>The reader shows a QR code and a six-character code. Scan the QR code with your phone,
      sign in to Tome if asked, check that the code matches and choose
      <strong>Connect reader</strong>. Without a camera, open <code>/link-reader</code> on your
      Tome server and type the code.</li>
    <li>A few seconds later the reader shows "Linked to" with your user name. Done.</li>
  </Steps>

  <h3>What arrives</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Each session with its book, start, end and reading time.</li>
    <li>How far you got. The book's progress in Tome follows it, forwards only.</li>
    <li>No page counts. The plugin system has none to send.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Good to know</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The ZIP holds your server's address and nothing about your account. It is the same for
      every user of your server.</li>
    <li>A connected reader gets a key of its own. It is listed under
      <strong>Settings → Access</strong> as "CrossPoint reader" and can be revoked there; the
      reader then asks you to sign in again and keeps its sessions until you do.</li>
    <li><strong>Settings → Xteink readers</strong> shows the connected readers and when the last
      session arrived. Opening <strong>Plugins → Tome</strong> on the reader shows the same.</li>
    <li>The reader needs a saved Wi-Fi network from which it can reach your Tome server. A
      session read without one waits on the reader and is sent later.</li>
    <li>The reader keeps a small queue, about a dozen sessions. If it cannot reach Tome for
      longer than that, the firmware clears the queue and those sessions are gone. On CrossInk
      the built-in sync has no such limit.</li>
    <li>On CrossPoint 2.0.0 a book whose path on the card is longer than about 230 characters
      produces no session. That is a limit of the firmware; CrossInk allows longer paths.</li>
    <li>Session times come from the reader's clock. On some readers that clock has been
      reported to run ahead, and Tome stores the times as sent.</li>
    <li>On CrossInk the plugin can run next to the built-in sync. A session that arrives both
      ways counts once.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="built-in">The built-in sync (CrossInk only, experimental)</h2>
  <p>
    CrossInk 2.0 can send its reading to Tome over the KOReader Sync account it already uses
    for progress. You start the sync on the reader.
  </p>
  <Steps>
    <li>Set a sync password in <strong>Settings → Access</strong> if you have none. An account
      registered from the reader itself is not tied to a Tome user and gets no stats.</li>
    <li>On the reader, set the KOReader Sync server to <code>https://your-server/api/v1</code>
      with your Tome username and the sync password (<strong>Settings → Xteink readers</strong> shows
      them to copy), and <strong>Authenticate</strong>. That is
      when it checks what the server supports.</li>
    <li>Turn on <strong>Reading Stats</strong> under <strong>What to Sync</strong>, then sync.{' '}
      <strong>Clippings</strong> can be switched on there too.</li>
  </Steps>

  <h3>What arrives</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Each session with its book, start, end and active reading time. It counts in the stats
      pages, the calendar and streaks.</li>
    <li>The position in the open book, and with it the progress line on the book's page.</li>
    <li>A page count per book (see below).</li>
    <li>The finished flag: when the reader reports a book as finished, Tome marks it as read
      with the reader's finish date.</li>
    <li>Clippings, if switched on (see below).</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>How pages are counted</h3>
  <p>
    Sessions arrive with time but no pages. The reader sends one page total per book, and Tome
    turns its growth between two syncs into pages for the sessions read in between, shared out
    by reading time and marked with a small sign as attributed.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Sync after each sitting and every session gets its exact pages. Sync less often and a
      larger total is spread over more sessions.</li>
    <li>A book's all-time <strong>Pages</strong> and <strong>Pace</strong> always match the
      reader's counter.</li>
    <li>For a book that is new on the reader, the first sync gives its pages to the sessions
      sent with it. For a book the reader had counted long before, the first count is only the
      starting point.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Reading from before the first sync</h3>
  <p>
    That reading has no sessions. The reader keeps lifetime totals and a calendar of read days
    and sends them with every sync. The days show on the <strong>Calendar</strong> as reading
    days without a time and count for streaks. The Stats page set to <strong>All</strong>{' '}
    includes the earlier time, sessions and pages, marked "before sync".
  </p>

  <h3>Good to know</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sync Book covers the open book only:</strong> its position and its page count.
      Reading time is sent for every book. After finishing one book and starting the next,
      sync once from inside each of them.</li>
    <li><strong>One server at a time:</strong> while the reader points at Tome it sends nothing
      to CrossPoint Sync, and reading it already sent there is not sent to Tome.</li>
    <li><strong>A book Tome can't identify:</strong> its sessions count toward your totals and
      are listed as "(book not linked yet)". They appear on the calendar once the file is
      linked: by itself for a book you downloaded from Tome or, with{' '}
      <strong>Send Document Metadata</strong> on, for any book (see{' '}
      <a href={withBase("/docs/sync-clients")}>KOSync apps</a>), or by hand with{' '}
      <em>Link KOReader sync</em> on the book's page.</li>
    <li><strong>Your edits stay:</strong> a session you trim or delete in Tome stays that way,
      even when the reader sends it again.</li>
    <li><strong>Known firmware bug:</strong> on CrossInk 2.0.0-rc, <strong>Sync Reading
      Stats</strong> for more than one book at a time reports a failure with any server. The
      data still arrives, and syncing from inside a book works.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Clippings (experimental)</h3>
  <p>
    A clipping is a passage you save on the reader. With <strong>Clippings</strong> switched on
    under <strong>What to Sync</strong>, the reader uploads its clippings to Tome and restores
    the ones made on your other CrossInk readers; a clipping deleted on one reader is removed
    everywhere. In Tome they appear on the <strong>Highlights</strong> page and in the book's
    <em>Highlights and notes</em>, marked as CrossInk clippings, as soon as the file is linked
    to a book. They are read-only here: change or delete them on the reader. They are not sent
    to KOReader devices and the iOS app does not show them yet.
  </p>

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>CrossInk shows stats as "Not supported"</strong>: it remembers the answer from
      the last time you authenticated. Set the sync password in <strong>Settings → Access</strong>,
      then authenticate on the reader again.</li>
    <li><strong>The plugin sends nothing</strong>: check that Plugins is turned on, that the
      folder on the card is <code>/plugins/tome</code> with <code>config.json</code> in it, that
      <strong>Plugins → Tome</strong> on the reader says it is linked, and that the reader has a
      saved Wi-Fi network from which it reaches your server.</li>
    <li><strong>The reader says the sign-in failed</strong>: a code lasts ten minutes. Choose
      <strong>Sign in</strong> again for a new one. The address in <code>config.json</code> must
      be one your phone can open too, since the QR code points at it.</li>
    <li><strong>A session shows as "(book not linked yet)"</strong>: Tome does not know which
      book the file is. Link it with <em>Link KOReader sync</em> on the book's page.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
